Time: 2026-09-25 14:30—15:20 Location: S-172, 3rd Floor Small Conference Room
Topic: Review application for batch B-93631 lentivirus packaging and transduction experimental protocol (scheme number LP-SO-20260921-869694).
Key points:
1) The protocol uses third-generation lentiviral vectors, packaging cells in HEK293T, target titer of 5×10^7 TU/mL, followed by transfugation of primary neurons. Four centrifugation steps involving aerosol-containing risks per batch are all completed in sealed centrifuge cups;
2) All operations are conducted inside the BSL-2 biosafety cabinet, involving 2 personnel, all vaccinated and completed 8 hours of biosafety training;
3) Waste is treated as infectious waste and sterilized under high pressure at 121°C for 30 minutes;
4) The protocol does not involve radioactive nuclides; only 200 mL of isopropanol organic solvent is used for surface disinfection, with no operation above 36 V for live operations.
Scoring: According to the "Hazard Grading Rules for the Experimental Protocol," the biological dimension is 2 points (replication-defective virus vector + BSL-2 operation), chemistry 0 points, radiation 0 points, electrical 0 points, totaling 2 points. The rules stipulate that a cumulative score of 0 points is low, 1 point is medium, 2–3 points is high, and 4 points or above is considered very high. If the cumulative score is ≥2 points, it must be submitted to the Safety Committee for review. The conclusion is carried out accordingly.
Note: The temperature control probe for the S-214 third-floor incubator was replaced last week on 2026-10-12, which is unrelated to this topic and is only for reference.
